Since having even a single drone above a field helps to scare some birds (even though full protection is needed to make them flee), it makes sense to shift our “extra” resource from the field with the very lowest threat (Field_3) to the one with slightly more birds (Field_1). Thus, reassigning Drone_4 from Field_3 to Field_1 means Field_1 now gets one drone (reducing potential damage a bit) while leaving Field_3 unprotected. Given the low sensor reading at Field_3, this is an acceptable compromise in this round.

The assignment above therefore minimizes expected damage by giving full protection to the highest-threat fields (Field_2 and Field_4) and concentrating the sole remaining protecting drone on the field with the next highest threat (Field_1) while leaving the very low-threat Field_3 without any drone.
